	(text "Power switch: SW3 pulls the gate of Q2 to GND = ON, the other position leaves the gate to R17 = OFF. SW3 pin 1 stays open so the switch can never short the battery.\nVSYS = switched battery voltage (4.0-6.4 V): motors (DRV8833) and servos (eFuse) run from it directly,\nthe logic gets it through a Schottky diode (see Power Conversion)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1c5e3107-e352-4910-b167-60a0d532dc9b")
	)
	(text "Battery voltage divider on VSYS (after SW3, 4x AA, 1:3): reads 0 V when the power switch is off\n6.4 V new alkaline   -> 2.13 V\n5.8 V NiMH, charged -> 1.93 V\n4.8 V NiMH nominal -> 1.60 V\n4.0 V empty (1.0 V/cell) -> 1.33 V\nIO3 = ADC1_CH2 (works while Wi-Fi is on)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 204.978 110.236 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a962af0d-c862-4bd7-b43f-14f43f912021")
	)
	(text "Battery (J2, JST-XH 2-pin, 3 A): flat 4x AA holder under the board, leads soldered to a JST-XH pigtail.\nPin 1 = + (red), pin 2 = - (black). NiMH 1900-2500 mAh (4.0 V empty ... 5.8 V charged, about 3 h) or alkaline (up to 6.4 V new).\nCharge the cells in an external AA charger; the board never charges them (alkalines must never be charged).\nF1 (resettable fuse, 3 A hold / 5 A trip) protects against shorts; switch off and on to reset it.\nQ1 (P-FET, gate to GND) blocks a reversed holder plug."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 119.38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b1578088-7a23-47b9-9f22-9a0c846a12e2")
	)
